          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"sampling-convergence-and-performance\">Sampling, convergence and performance</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Compare PXR/CBS yields for three sampled-history budgets and one\nadaptive stopping policy. All runs use a 30 keV beam, 100 nm HOPG,\n135\u00b0 observation, and no bremsstrahlung.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The <strong>600\u20132,000 eV</strong> band integral is less noisy than individual grid\nsamples. Small CPU budgets illustrate the method, not validated precision;\nsampled histories are not physical bunch charge.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
