          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"interpretation\">Interpretation</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The largest fixed-budget yield is only a reference, <strong>not ground truth</strong>.\nThese runs share a resolved default seed, so their differences are not\nan independent-sample error estimate. For uncertainty, use independent\nseeds and inspect the convergence diagnostics.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">An adaptive run may stop at its maximum without achieving its RSE\ntarget; check its diagnostics. Changing reflection families or energy\ngrids tests systematic discretization, not sampling convergence.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Wall times depend on compilation, caching and hardware. The untimed\nwarmup helps, but these are <strong>not portable benchmarks</strong>. Try increasing\nthe budgets and compare the <a href=\"https://pyrite.readthedocs.io/en/latest/reference/python-api/config.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">sampling reference</a>\nand <a href=\"https://pyrite.readthedocs.io/en/latest/computation/index.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">performance guidance</a>.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
